---
import { getCollection, render } from "astro:content";
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import scripts from "../../data/replication-scripts.json";
import { replicationSection, referenceSection } from "../../sidebars";

const pages = (await getCollection("replication")).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const sidebar = [await replicationSection(), referenceSection()];

const cards = await Promise.all(
  pages.map(async (p) => {
    const { headings } = await render(p);
    return {
      id: p.id,
      title: p.data.title,
      blurb: p.data.blurb,
      methods: headings.filter((h) => h.depth === 2).length,
      scripts: scripts.filter((s) => s.family === p.id).length,
    };
  }),
);
---

<DocsLayout
  eyebrow="The replication record"
  title="Replication"
  description="Every method exuber implements beyond the original PSY test was read from its primary source, implemented, and then independently re-derived by a standalone script. This is that record — what was reproduced, how, and where it fell short."
  sidebar={sidebar}
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      The pages below are the working research behind <code>exuber</code>'s post-PSY
      surface, organised by methodological family. Each one states the primary source,
      what the method actually does, which published numbers were reproduced exactly,
      what was deliberately simplified relative to the paper, and what remains open.
    </p>
    <p>
      Validation is kept separate from the test suite on purpose. The package's own
      <code>testthat</code> tests guard against regression; the scripts collected here
      re-derive each statistic from scratch — brute-force <code>lm()</code> fits,
      hand-telescoped identities, Monte Carlo size and power — so that agreement means
      something independent of the implementation being checked. Several of them found
      real bugs, and those are recorded rather than quietly fixed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every script is self-contained and depends on none of the others. Run one from the
      <code>exuber/</code> package root, or adjust the <code>devtools::load_all()</code>
      call at its top:
    </p>
    <pre class="astro-code"><code>Rscript docs/enhancements/replication/monitoring/radf_cusum_validation.R</code></pre>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border bg-border sm:grid-cols-2">
    {
      cards.map((c) => (
        <a
          href={`/replication/${c.id}`}
          class="group flex flex-col gap-3 bg-panel p-6 transition-colors hover:bg-panel-hi"
        >
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-ink">{c.title}</h2>
            <span class="shrink-0 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
              {c.methods} {c.methods === 1 ? "section" : "sections"}
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{c.blurb}</p>
          {c.scripts > 0 && (
            <span class="mt-auto font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-stable">
              {c.scripts} replication {c.scripts === 1 ? "script" : "scripts"}
            </span>
          )}
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Cited PDFs are not redistributed here — the bibliography carries DOIs and working-paper
    links instead. Earlier implementations (STADF, kernel-purge, SBZ, common-bubble, root
    inference, PDC) were validated before this convention started and have no archived script.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
